nReturn just the location(s)\n\nNote: Your thinking should be thorough and so it's fine if it's very long.\n\n--- BEGIN PROBLEM STATEMENT ---\nTitle: [WIP] : Added assert_consistent_docs() and related tests\n\nFixes #9388 \r\n\r\nAdded a function to check for consistency between docstring of objects.\r\n\r\nIn this approach there is a python dictionary for each of Parameters, Attributes and Returns. Indexed by the name of the parameter/attribute/return with the value being a Python dictionary containing its type definition and description. The function checks for each object if the docstring is identical (excluding whitespaces) for a given parameter/attribute/return in the main dictionary. If a new parameter/attribute/return are found they are added in the main dictionary.\n--- END PROBLEM STATEMENT ---\n\nIMPORTANT: You should ONLY interact with the environment provided to you AND NEVER ASK FOR HUMAN HELP.\nDon't include any lambda functions!\nYou should NOT modify any files!\n"}, {"content": "I'll help analyze this issue systematically according to the given steps.\n\n## Step 1: Categorize and Extract Key Information\nKey terms to search for:\n- \"assert_consistent_docs\"\n- \"docstring\" validation/check\"\n- \"Parameters\", \"Attributes\", \"Returns\" doc sections\n- Related testing infrastructure\n\nLet me search for relevant code:\n\n<function=search_code_snippets>\n<parameter=search_terms>['assert_consistent_docs', 'docstring']</parameter>\n", "role": "assistant", "tool_calls": null, "function_call": null}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "toolu_01", "name": "search_code_snippets", "content": "OBSERVATION:\nsklearn/utils/validation.py:_to_object_array\nsklearn/cross_decomposition/_pls.py:_pinv2_old\nsklearn/cross_decomposition/_pls.py:_get_first_singular_vectors_power_method\nsklearn/cross_decomposition/_pls.py:_center_scale_xy\nsklearn/cross_decomposition/_pls.py:_get_first_singular_vectors_svd\nsklearn/cross_decomposition/_pls.py:_svd_flip_1d\nsklearn/cros