the marker. Possible values:\n4774 | \n4775 |             - 'face': The edge color will always be the same as the face color.\n4776 |             - 'none': No patch boundary will be drawn.\n4777 |             - A color or sequence of colors.\n4778 | \n4779 |             For non-filled markers, *edgecolors* is ignored. Instead, the color\n4780 |             is determined like with 'face', i.e. from *c*, *colors*, or\n4781 |             *facecolors*.\n4782 | \n4783 |         %(colorizer_doc)s\n4784 | \n4785 |             This parameter is ignored if *c* is RGB(A).\n4786 | \n4787 |         plotnonfinite : bool, default: False\n4788 |             Whether to plot points with nonfinite *c* (i.e. ``inf``, ``-inf``\n4789 |             or ``nan``). If ``True`` the points are drawn with the *bad*\n4790 |             colormap color (see `.Colormap.set_bad`).\n4791 | \n4792 |         Returns\n4793 |         -------\n4794 |         `~matplotlib.collections.PathCollection`\n4795 | \n4796 |         Other Parameters\n4797 |         ----------------\n4798 |         data : indexable object, optional\n4799 |             DATA_PARAMETER_PLACEHOLDER\n4800 |         **kwargs : `~matplotlib.collections.Collection` properties\n4801 | \n4802 |         See Also\n4803 |         --------\n4804 |         plot : To plot scatter plots when markers are identical in size and\n4805 |             color.\n4806 | \n4807 |         Notes\n4808 |         -----\n4809 |         * The `.plot` function will be faster for scatterplots where markers\n4810 |           don't vary in size or color.\n4811 | \n4812 |         * Any or all of *x*, *y*, *s*, and *c* may be masked arrays, in which\n4813 |           case all masks will be combined and only unmasked points will be\n4814 |           plotted.\n4815 | \n4816 |         * Fundamentally, scatter works with 1D arrays; *x*, *y*, *s*, and *c*\n4817 |           may be input as N-D arrays, but within scatter they will be\n4818 |           flattened. The exception is 